cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, formal proofs, datasets, or white papers, please cite them using these metadata."
title: "human-synapse-bouton-lab: Human Synaptic Bouton Model Workbench with Lean-Checked Elementary Model Invariants, Stochastic Nanocolumn Simulator, and Open-Problems Survey"
abstract: "A multi-language (TypeScript, Rust, Python, Lean 4.35.0) computational workbench for a human synaptic bouton model. Lean 4.35.0 kernel-checks 24 elementary integer and list-induction lemmas about the repository's own model formulas, with 27 non-vacuity witnesses and 6 sanity checks; these are known elementary facts and resolve no published open question. The repository also includes a 50-digit reference oracle, a pre-registered Monte Carlo release simulator whose results are properties of chosen, illustrative parameters, and two white papers surveying open problems in 11 disciplines with a crosswalk to the Unsolved Problems Mega-Atlas (0 of 1,900 problems solved)."
